Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 10:30:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] tests(RI-23a): coder_escalation declares its :8083 host's
 thinking kwargs; alias/host guard

The lean registry's server_mode.coder_escalation.chat_template_kwargs becomes
{enable_thinking: true, reasoning_effort: medium} (research lane/ri23a-20260929).
- test_chat_template_kwargs_for_role_reads_server_mode expects that value.
- New test_alias_thinking_kwarg_agrees_with_its_host: a shared_with alias whose
  request-side enable_thinking disagrees with its host's fails. The stack priors
  derive an alias's thinking state from its host, so a disagreeing alias is
  admitted to the RI-23 chat lane as a thinking role and then sent
  enable_thinking=false. Fails on the pre-RI-23a lean (checked), passes after.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FKXdQsgLuwnFVWQ3npGfrJ
